name: Git baseline history cannot imply complete coverage or a fixed finding
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/source_baselines.py @TMP_TARGET @ART prepare @TMP_HOME
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 SETUP · READY THE MAP RUN | ready
submit: run coverage:baselines {}
wait: 0.5
submit: logs
keys: End
require-live-snap: 25 Historical Git baseline records: 3 | baseline-records
expect: synthetic-not-a-scan
submit: run coverage:sweep {}
wait: 0.5
submit: logs
keys: End
require-live-snap: 25 scope is unavailable | clean-baseline-check
expect: baseline was captured dirty
expect: tracked source unchanged
ask: Does the receipt distinguish unchanged tracked source, a dirty historical baseline and an unavailable scope, with full SHAs and no claim of complete coverage or a fixed finding?
nav-mode:
keys: z
require-live-snap: 20 READ TRANSCRIPT | reader
resize: 160x48
live-snap: reader-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: reader-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: reader-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: reader-60x20
resize: 40x12
live-snap: reader-40x12
keys: End
live-snap: reader-tail-40x12
keys: PPage
live-snap: reader-page-40x12
ask: Are source identities and their limitations readable through the transcript controls at all six sizes without losing navigation?
keys: q
resize: 120x36
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/source_baselines.py @TMP_TARGET @ART dirty
submit: run coverage:sweep {}
wait: 0.5
submit: logs
keys: End
require-live-snap: 25 working tree is dirty | same-sha-dirty
expect: 3 source unverified
submit: run coverage:sweep {"writeSkips":true}
wait: 0.5
submit: logs
keys: End
require-live-snap: 25 dirty tree | dirty-skip-refused
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/source_baselines.py @TMP_TARGET @ART committed
submit: run coverage:sweep {}
wait: 0.5
submit: logs
keys: End
require-live-snap: 25 source changed: 1 file(s) | new-sha-changed
expect: baseline was captured dirty
submit: setup
require-live-snap: 25 SETUP · READY THE MAP RUN | setup-still-needed
expect-not: Map ✓
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/source_baselines.py @TMP_TARGET @ART after
ask: Does a same-SHA edit remain unverified, refuse skip writes and then disclose the changed source after an owned commit, without creating investigation work?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 SETUP · READY THE MAP RUN | restarted
submit: run coverage:sweep {}
wait: 0.5
submit: logs
keys: End
require-live-snap: 25 source changed: 1 file(s) | restarted-source-history
submit: setup
require-live-snap: 25 SETUP · READY THE MAP RUN | restarted-setup
expect-not: Map ✓
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/source_baselines.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
ask: Does no-color restart preserve historical records and require genuine Map work, with zero provider requests, scans, findings and decisions?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
